      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اشذى</span></b>  <i>He annoyed, molested, harmed,</i> or
<i>hurt:</i> or <i>he did what annoyed, molested, harmed,</i>
or <i>hurt:</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آذى</span>: (S, Msb, TA:) and (TA) so
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذَا</span></b> , (K,) aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذُوَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذًا</span>, (TA,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذْوٌ</span>.
(TK [accord. to which the latter verb is trans.].)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اشذاهُ عَنْهُ</span>, (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِشْذَآءٌ</span>, (TA,) <i>He
put aside,</i> or <i>away,</i> and <i>removed far off, him,</i> or
<i>it, from him,</i> or <i>it.</i> (K, TA.)

